# What must never enter the build context.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters and it is not about image size: the
# build stage does `COPY . .` on top of an already-installed workspace, so a
# host `node_modules` would overwrite the Linux install with whatever was built
# on the developer's machine. On Windows that means Windows binaries for sharp
# and @node-rs/argon2, and a container that fails at runtime with a module it
# can see but cannot load.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Stale artefacts from a host build would be copied over and
# then partially overwritten, which is worse than either alone.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. `.env` holds a real DATABASE_URL and .tokens.json holds live
# session credentials; neither belongs in an image layer, where it survives
# even if a later layer deletes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.tokens.json
.token

.git
.github
coverage
demo/preview
.media
*.log
